  "summary_en": "Commission staff working document monitoring implementation of the European Declaration on Digital Rights and Principles in 2024–25. It uses Eurobarometer data and an impact indicator framework to assess Member State initiatives across six chapters, covering the AI Act, DSA, DMA and Data Act. Robots appear only in passing, in a survey figure on attitudes to robots and AI at work.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Over 2,000 initiatives implementing digital rights were identified across the EU-27.",
   "The indicator framework estimates digital rights are effectively applied at only 61% on average.",
   "The AI Act bans took effect in February 2025 and GPAI obligations follow in August 2025.",
   "Biggest gaps are in freedom of choice, participation in the digital public space and sustainability.",
   "A Digital Fairness Act proposal is expected in the second half of 2026."
  ],
